    "title": "Sterling and Rock Falls Fire Training Together Gets Closer - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Tom Katz ,\n14 hours ago The Sterling and Rock Falls fire departments have been awarded an $825,000 federal grant to construct a regional fire training tower. This initiative comes in response to the tragic 2021 line-of-duty death of Sterling Lt. Garrett Ramos. The planned facility will provide realistic, scenario-based training to better prepare firefighters for emergencies. Officials say the tower will enhance safety and effectiveness across the region. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
